title: The Town Hall at Mülheim
subtitle: Unemployed workers take over a town in the occupied Ruhr.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1923 and month = 4
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
RG.news('Red flag over the town hall of Mülheim', 2);
!}

= The Town Hall at Mülheim

In Mülheim an der Ruhr a march of the unemployed against the price of bread ends at the town hall and stays there. The German police, half of them expelled by the French, are nowhere to be seen. A committee of local communists and syndicalists declares that it will run the food supply until prices fall. The Ruhr district asks the Zentrale for orders and for money.

- @spread: Every Ruhr town its own committee.
- @bargain: Hold the town hall and negotiate the prices.
- @withdraw: Get our members out before it ends in blood.

@spread
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] A test of strength months early. The committees will stay in being.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids armed seizures.
