Committees of action appear in Gelsenkirchen and Bochum. The employers and the Social Democratic mayors raise volunteer police, and the committees are cleared one town at a time. They meet again the following week in the miners' pubs.

@bargain
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. Fixed prices for bread, and a procession out with banners.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have nothing to send.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
RG.district('ruhr', {loyalty: 5, members: 0.04});
Q.e23_mulheim = 2;
Q.worker_support += 3;
!}

Our delegation, the town council and the union secretaries agree on fixed prices for bread and potatoes. The committee leaves the town hall in procession.

@withdraw
subtitle: No dead. The Ruhr Left will not forgive it.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district('ruhr', {militancy: -6, loyalty: -8});
Q.e23_mulheim = 3;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 8;
!}

The Zentrale orders the comrades out. Most obey. The syndicalists stay and are arrested on the third night.
